16. Human Oversight Gate

Automatic publication of high‑confidence results is unsafe. We insert a mandatory human‑in‑the‑loop gate as a formal AND‑condition.

Definition 16.1 (Publication Gate). A verified output A \in \mathcal{V}_\alpha is published only if

\text{Publish}(A) = \mathbf{1}_{A \in \mathcal{V}_\alpha} \;\cdot\; \mathbf{1}_{\text{HumanExpert}(A) = \text{accept}}.

Thus membership in \mathcal{V}_\alpha is necessary but not sufficient. This directly closes the gap identified in early critiques: no output reaches the world without human judgement, regardless of its machine‑computed risk score.

