17. Explicit Assumptions Register (A1–A8)

Every theorem in this chapter depends on a subset of the following assumptions. These are not hidden; they are the declared preconditions for each guarantee.

Label Assumption
A1 Exchangeability of calibration and test data (Theorem 7.1).
A2 Measurability: \Omega is a set, \mathcal{F} a \sigma-algebra, all propositions are measurable (Sections 2–3).
A3 Exchangeable and non‑adversarially ordered evidence stream for convergence (Theorem 13.1) or exchangeability plus bounded reliability for robust convergence (Assumptions 9.A).
