21. Conclusion

We have constructed a single, mathematically rigorous object that instantiates every box in the “Knowledge → Belief → Reasoning → Verified Output” pipeline. The formalism separates truth, belief, logic, and confidence; provides a provably unique consistent update rule; calibrates outputs with distribution‑free guarantees; and unifies multiple sources of epistemic risk into a single budget. The gap between exact Bayesian convergence and robust, scalable inference has been closed with a dedicated convergence theorem for the trust‑weighted generalised posterior. Information geometry gives a natural, optimal gradient for belief transport. Hardness results enforce an honest tractability boundary.

The chapter concludes with an explicit assumptions register and a frank catalogue of limitations. This is not a weakness — it is the mathematical honesty that a truth‑seeking intelligence requires. The next chapter, “Verified Multi‑Agent Intelligence”, will use multiple independent instances of this architecture to cross‑examine each other’s assumptions, precisely targeting the seams we have left open.

